              </article>
            </div>
            <a class="btn btn-fill btn-block" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=112+S+Carroll+Ave+Dallas+TX+75226">Directions</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="order" class="band rise" aria-labelledby="order-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="order-panel">
            <p class="eyebrow light">Order</p>
            <h2 id="order-title">Order for pickup</h2>
            <p class="order-lead">Cash only. No delivery.</p>
            <form id="order-form">
              <div class="field">
                <label for="order-name">Name</label>
                <input id="order-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required />
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="order-phone">Phone</label>
                <input id="order-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required />
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="order-day">Pickup day</label>
                <input id="order-day" name="day" type="date" required />
              </div>
              <div class="field">
                <label for="order-want">What they want</label>
                <textarea id="order-want" name="order" required></textarea>
              </div>
              <p class="order-note">Cash only.</p>
              <button class="btn btn-white" type="submit">Place pickup order</button>
            </form>
            <p id="order-result" class="order-result" hidden>
              This is a demo, so this order stays on the page. To order for real, call <a href="tel:+12148231719">(214) 823-1719</a>. Cash only.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="reviews" class="band blush rise" aria-labelledby="reviews-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">Reviews</p>
          <h2 id="reviews-title">Reviews</h2>
          <div class="review-grid">
        <article class="card review">
          <p class="stars">5 stars</p>
          <h3>Adam Abam</h3>
          <p class="when">11 months ago</p>
          <p>Authentic and delicious!</p>
          <p>Graciela’s Bakery is one of those hidden gems that reminds you of home. The mexican pan dulce is always fresh especially the conchas, which are soft, fluffy, and full of flavor. You can really taste the love and tradition in every bite. The family who runs the bakery is kind and welcoming, and the prices are super fair. It’s small, cozy, and full of good vibes. If you want real, traditional Mexican sweet bread in Dallas, this is the place! Highly recommended! 💛🥖☕️</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card review">
          <p class="stars">5 stars</p>
          <h3>Lina Juarez</h3>
          <p class="when">4 months ago</p>
          <p>Omg ! Both ladies are sooo sweet ! The bread with some cafecito was amazing, not super sweet but so moist and cooked with so much love ! If you want some pan dulce, definitely stop by here !!</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card review">
          <p class="stars">5 stars</p>
          <h3>Maria Arriaga</h3>
          <p class="when">a year ago</p>
          <p>Que rico! So nostalgia in here. Delicioso pan dulce. Lovely spot y la señora Graciela is so sweet and kind. She was down to have a conversation about her business and making pan dulce. Come out and support if you are near the area. Cash only.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card review">
          <p class="stars">5 stars</p>
          <h3>Paul</h3>
          <p class="when">6 months ago</p>
          <p>I had to check this little place out after seeing their videos I'm so glad I went only been two times but I'm going to be a regular from now on passing up dozens of Mexican bakeries on the way just to get my pan dulce from Gracielas on Carroll holiday pan and cookies are cool and so good everything tastes great heat a lil bit and tastes like just out the oven very friendly family owned and run I've never had to wait and they always have a good selection of treats and very reasonable prices. This is my go to spot for pan dulce now 👍👍👍👍👍👍⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card review">
          <p class="stars">5 stars</p>
          <h3>Wendy Oviedo</h3>
          <p class="when">11 months ago</p>
          <p>I have been visiting Graciela’s Bakery off and on within the last 20 years. I am always treated like family and the quality of the pan dulce is fresh, tasty and you can feel the love baked into it. My parents will usually ask when I’m going to visit the bakery because they of course love the pan dulce from there too. I went in today and had the chance to try their new tortuga conchas! They are so cute and smell divine. I came in specifically for pan de muerto to decorate my ofrenda for day of the dead, so this was truly an added treat. I love Graciela’s Bakery, I hope you make the trip to try their pan dulce, I’m confident you’ll love them too!</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card review">
          <p class="stars">5 stars</p>
          <h3>Fajita Pita</h3>
          <p class="when">a year ago</p>
          <p>I had pan dulce from Gracielas Bakery at an event this past Friday.  The pan dulce was on the cake table and the vibrant colors were the first thing that caught my eyes.  I impatiently waited for us to be allowed to eat some and when we did the concha was SOFT and DELICIOUS! I was lucky and scored a few pieces to take home and even now a few days after the event the bread is still delicious and soft.</p>
          <p>I highly recommend this bakery and will always try to support a family owned business.</p>
        </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="close rise" aria-label="Hours">
        <p>Cash only. Open every day, 7am to 7pm.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-white" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=112+S+Carroll+Ave+Dallas+TX+75226">Directions</a>
      </section>
